 "brief": "The turret for my robot arm's base, PETG, printed with its base on the bed (layers along +Z).\nIt bolts down onto a slewing ring: the bottom of the part is a flat ring 70 mm OD / 50 mm ID,\n4 mm thick (z = 0 to 4), with six M3 clearance holes on a 60 mm bolt circle (the first one on\n+X, every 60 degrees). Above it, two uprights carry the shoulder shaft: a 10 mm shaft along Y at\nz = 50, passing through 10.2 mm holes at y = +25 and y = -25 (each upright has a boss at least\n4 mm of wall round its hole, 8 mm long along Y, from |y| = 21 to 29). The shoulder servo sits\nbetween the uprights: x = -20 to 20, y = -18 to 18, z = 8 to 62 stays clear. The part has to\nstay within a 40 mm radius of the Z axis and below z = 62. The arm it carries weighs 1.5 kg with\nits centre of mass 150 mm out along +X from the shaft; it also slews, with up to 1 N\u00b7m about Z.\nSafety factor 2.",
